window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-f094a985d5b867ef"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"using-the-admin-plugin-in-chatgpt-work\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"chatgpt-work-admin\">在 ChatGPT Work 中使用 Admin 插件</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引见 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code> 可获取 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>本指南介绍 Admin 插件如何协助常见管理工作、如何为任务做好准备，以及如何在获得适当审批并提供充分上下文的情况下尝试关键用例。</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=29SyCndnMZs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">观看：在 ChatGPT Work 中使用 Admin 插件（需联网）</a></p> <p><a id=\"1-understand-what-the-admin-plugin-is-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"1-admin\">1. 了解 Admin 插件的用途</h2> <p>Admin 插件旨在帮助你直接在 ChatGPT Work 中管理设置、权限和控制项。你用日常语言说明目标后，插件会收集所需输入、读取当前状态、解释查询结果，并引导你采取下一项受支持的步骤。</p> <p><a id=\"what-the-admin-plugin-is-designed-to-solve\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"admin\">Admin 插件旨在解决的问题</h3> <ul> <li>将管理请求转化为清晰的工作流程，无需你编写 API 请求。</li> <li>在作出决定或批准变更前，先检查当前工作区状态。</li> <li>显示哪些获准来源和字段支持结论，以及哪些内容无法核实。</li> <li>在执行受支持的变更前暂停以供审核；变更后再读取记录以确认结果。</li> </ul> <p>该插件在后台使用选定的管理 API 和已批准的连接数据源。它不会把所有管理系统合并在一起、扩大你的权限，也不会让你在 ChatGPT 中使用所有 API 操作。数据所属的系统仍决定插件可以读取或修改哪些内容。</p> <p><a id=\"what-admin-apis-are-designed-to-solve\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"api\">管理 API 的用途</h3> <p>管理 API 为软件提供一种结构化方式，以请求数据或执行受支持的操作。组织可以使用管理 API 构建内部流程或外部工具。常见用途包括定期报告、跨大量记录重复执行工作，以及连接到已批准的系统。此类工作流程通常需要经过工程、安全和治理审查。</p> <p>使用本指南不需要构建 API 工作流程。指南其余部分聚焦于 Admin 插件。ChatGPT 工作区管理与 OpenAI API Platform 管理彼此独立，各自有不同的权限和身份验证要求。</p> <p><a id=\"keep-credentials-private\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_1\">妥善保护凭据</h3> <p>仅使用组织批准的连接和密钥存储系统。切勿把真实的管理员 API 密钥粘贴到 ChatGPT、Codex、文档或源代码文件中。</p> <p><a id=\"2-prepare-to-use-the-admin-plugin\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"2-admin\">2. 准备使用 Admin 插件</h2> <p>如果要用日常语言完成一项受支持的一次性任务，可以使用 Admin 插件。说明目标，并提供稳定 ID 或已批准的报告上下文。插件会在你决定是否继续前，显示它查到的内容或准备进行的变更。</p> <p>插件只会使用该任务获准的来源、凭据和操作，不会合并所有管理系统，也不会扩大你的权限。原始系统仍是事实来源。</p> <p><a id=\"before-you-begin\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_2\">开始之前</h3> <ol> <li>找到记录所在的管理区域。</li> <li>准备所需输入并确认已取得审批。</li> <li>从只读请求开始。</li> <li>询问插件使用了哪些来源和字段，以及有哪些内容无法核实。</li> <li>对于受支持的变更，先检查计划再批准；随后要求插件重新读取记录并确认结果。</li> </ol> <p>确认你的工作区中已启用该插件，且你拥有所需权限。下文有关角色和访问权限的用例反映插件当前文档所述的功能范围。插件可以查看角色、功能权限，以及用户或群组分配情况。得到你的确认后，它还可以将一个现有角色分配给一个现有群组。</p> <p>插件不能创建角色、修改角色权限，也不能确认对某个特定连接器的访问权限。</p> <p>分析类用例需要访问已连接且获准使用的数据源。ROI 分析还需要已批准的业务或工程结果数据；仅有使用记录还不够。</p> <p><a id=\"3-explore-key-admin-plugin-use-cases\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"3-admin\">3. 探索 Admin 插件的关键用例</h2> <p>选择一个用例，将每个占位符替换为已批准请求中的值，并依序执行各步骤。除非任务是已获得批准的受支持变更，否则应从只读请求开始。下方保留英文提示原文供复制使用，并附中文参考译文。</p> <p>若要盘点 GPT、迁移符合条件的批次，并协调所有者测试和访问检查，请使用<a href=\"#/article/a-866d18fe9ed30c97?anchor=admin-bulk-migration\">批量迁移自定义 GPT</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"list-workspace-roles\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_3\">列出工作区角色</h3> <p><strong>可尝试的提示</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">List the roles in workspace {workspace_id}. Separate built-in and custom roles. For each role, explain which features it can use and show the users or groups assigned to it. Don’t make changes.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>中文参考：</strong> 列出工作区 {workspace_id} 中的角色。将内置角色和自定义角色分开。对于每个角色，说明它能使用哪些功能，并列出分配给它的用户或群组。不要进行更改。</p> <p><strong>步骤</strong></p> <ol> <li><strong>准备：</strong>确认工作区 ID，并确认你有权查看这些信息。</li> <li><strong>执行：</strong>请求只读角色列表。</li> <li><strong>审查：</strong>检查角色类型、功能访问权限和分配情况。</li> <li><strong>核实：</strong>如有意外情况，继续调查，但不要进行更改。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"review-one-role\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_4\">审查一个角色</h3> <p><strong>可尝试的提示</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Review role {role_id}. Explain its permissions in plain language, show who has it, and flag anything that looks broader than expected. Don’t edit the role.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>中文参考：</strong> 审查角色 {role_id}。用通俗语言解释它的权限，显示哪些人拥有该角色，并指出权限范围是否可能超出预期。不要编辑该角色。</p> <p><strong>步骤</strong></p> <ol> <li><strong>准备：</strong>确认角色 ID 和工作区。</li> <li><strong>执行：</strong>请求只读角色审查。</li> <li><strong>审查：</strong>检查权限和分配对象是否符合该角色的预期用途。</li> <li><strong>核实：</strong>记录要向角色所有者提出的问题。请记住，插件不能创建角色或修改其权限。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"understand-a-users-or-groups-access\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_5\">了解用户或群组的访问权限</h3> <p><strong>可尝试的提示</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Help me understand the access for user {user_id} or group {group_id}. Show their assigned roles, explain what access those roles provide, and point out overlaps or gaps. Clearly say what you can’t verify.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>中文参考：</strong> 帮我了解用户 {user_id} 或群组 {group_id} 的访问权限。列出他们已获分配的角色，说明这些角色提供哪些访问权限，并指出重叠或缺口。明确说明你无法核实的内容。</p> <p><strong>步骤</strong></p> <ol> <li><strong>准备：</strong>使用该用户或群组的稳定 ID。</li> <li><strong>执行：</strong>请插件解释其访问权限。</li> <li><strong>审查：</strong>检查分配了哪些角色以及这些角色提供什么访问权限，并注意重叠或缺口。</li> <li><strong>核实：</strong>如果插件看不到某项信息，应标记为未知，不要猜测。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"assign-an-existing-role-to-a-group\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_6\">将现有角色分配给群组</h3> <p><strong>可尝试的提示</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Before making a change, show the current roles for group {group_id} and explain what role {role_id} would add. Confirm the recorded approver and wait for my explicit approval. After the assignment, verify the group’s updated roles.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>中文参考：</strong> 更改前，先显示群组 {group_id} 当前拥有的角色，并说明添加角色 {role_id} 会带来什么权限。确认记录在案的审批人，并等待我明确批准。分配完成后，核实该群组更新后的角色。</p> <p><strong>步骤</strong></p> <ol> <li><strong>准备：</strong>确认群组 ID 和角色 ID，并检查已批准的请求以及记录在案的审批人。</li> <li><strong>执行：</strong>请插件显示当前角色以及计划变更内容。</li> <li><strong>审查：</strong>只有计划与已批准请求一致时才批准。</li> <li><strong>核实：</strong>分配完成后再次检查群组，确认已按批准内容添加现有角色。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"check-general-connector-permission\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_7\">检查一般连接器权限</h3> <p><strong>可尝试的提示</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Check whether user {user_id} has general connector access through their assigned roles. Ask the plugin to show which permissions support its answer. If it can’t verify access to a specific connector, have it say so clearly.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>中文参考：</strong> 检查用户 {user_id} 是否通过已分配的角色拥有一般连接器访问权限。请插件说明哪些权限支持它的结论。如果无法核实对某个特定连接器的访问权限，请明确说明。</p> <p><strong>步骤</strong></p> <ol> <li><strong>准备：</strong>确认用户 ID，以及你有权审查该用户访问权限。</li> <li><strong>执行：</strong>请求检查一般权限。</li> <li><strong>审查：</strong>检查已分配的角色，以及用于得出结论的权限。</li> <li><strong>核实：</strong>这只能作为一般性检查，不能证明用户可以访问某个具体连接器或已连接项目。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"troubleshoot-an-approved-change\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_8\">排查已批准的变更</h3> <p><strong>可尝试的提示</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Review approved change {change_record_id}. Compare the requested result with the current workspace. If it failed, check the workspace and role first. Then confirm who owns the record, explain the issue, and suggest the safest next step.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>中文参考：</strong> 审查已批准的变更 {change_record_id}。将请求的结果与当前工作区进行比较。如果变更失败，先检查工作区和角色；然后确认记录所有者、解释问题，并建议最安全的下一步。</p> <p><strong>步骤</strong></p> <ol> <li><strong>准备：</strong>确认已批准的变更记录及预期结果。</li> <li><strong>执行：</strong>请插件对照当前工作区检查请求。</li> <li><strong>审查：</strong>先检查工作区和角色，再核实记录所有者。</li> <li><strong>核实：</strong>采取下一步行动前，以当前工作区状态作为事实来源。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"optimize-cost-and-model-mix\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_9\">优化成本与模型组合</h3> <p><strong>可尝试的提示</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">For {date_range} in workspace {workspace_id}, group verified token use and cost by use case. Compare models and reasoning modes using the speed and quality information available. Flag costly workflows when the data shows little evidence of value. Recommend where spending could be reduced or redirected toward work with stronger productivity or cost results. Include any approved revenue or quality signals. Estimate possible savings, explain tradeoffs, and separate verified observations from assumptions or missing inputs. Keep this read-only.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>中文参考：</strong> 对工作区 {workspace_id} 在 {date_range} 期间的数据，按用例汇总已核实的词元用量和成本。根据现有的速度和质量信息比较模型与推理模式。如果数据几乎没有显示价值证据，请标记成本较高的工作流。建议可以在哪里削减支出，或将预算转向生产力或成本表现更好的工作。纳入任何已获批准的收入或质量指标。估算可能节省的金额、解释取舍，并区分已核实的观察与假设或缺失输入。保持只读。</p> <p><strong>步骤</strong></p> <ol> <li><strong>准备：</strong>确认工作区、日期范围和成本数据是否覆盖整个期间，并检查有哪些已批准的绩效或结果字段可用。</li> <li><strong>执行：</strong>请求比较成本和模型。</li> <li><strong>审查：</strong>区分数据直接显示的内容、假设、缺失输入和权衡因素。</li> <li><strong>核实：</strong>采取行动前，与财务部门及工作流程负责人核实可能节省的成本。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"discover-usage-and-adoption\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_10\">了解使用情况与采用情况</h3> <p><strong>可尝试的提示</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Analyze workspace {workspace_id} during {date_range}. Show tasks and token use by team and business function. Group cost by use case. Summarize what teams use ChatGPT and Codex to accomplish. Include examples from Legal, Marketing, and Sales. Compare available use of skills and plugins. Only report tool calls, connected apps, and multi-tool workflows if those fields are available. Show where teams use more advanced workflows and where there may be room to expand. Rank the top {5_or_10} use cases and show whether a small group of highly active users accounts for most usage. Don’t guess about activity that is not in the data.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>中文参考：</strong> 分析工作区 {workspace_id} 在 {date_range} 期间的数据。按团队和业务职能展示任务与词元用量，并按用例汇总成本。总结各团队使用 ChatGPT 和 Codex 完成的工作，举出法律、市场营销和销售方面的例子。比较可用的技能和插件用量。只有在相应字段可用时，才报告工具调用、已连接应用和多工具工作流。展示团队在哪些地方使用了更高级的工作流，以及还有哪些扩展空间。列出排名前 {5_or_10} 的用例，并说明是否有少数高活跃用户贡献了大部分用量。不要猜测数据中没有记录的活动。</p> <p><strong>步骤</strong></p> <ol> <li><strong>准备：</strong>检查工作区、日期范围和团队映射，并确认用户级报告已获批准。</li> <li><strong>执行：</strong>请求分析使用情况和采用情况。</li> <li><strong>审查：</strong>检查请求的字段哪些可用。缺失的活动数据应留空，不要猜测。</li> <li><strong>核实：</strong>高使用量并不能证明使用了高级功能、产生了业务价值或反映个人绩效。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"measure-business-value-and-roi\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"roi\">衡量业务价值和 ROI</h3> <p><strong>可尝试的提示</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">For workspace {workspace_id} in {date_range}, combine verified usage and cost with approved outcomes. Estimate value by team and use case. Include approved Sales measures for productivity, revenue, and quality. Compare teams and models, as well as workflows and user segments. Rank returns against cost. Show the sources and formula. Clearly state assumptions, limits, and missing inputs. Don’t claim ChatGPT caused the outcomes. Keep this read-only.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>中文参考：</strong> 对工作区 {workspace_id} 在 {date_range} 期间的数据，将已核实的使用情况和成本与获准使用的结果指标结合起来，按团队和用例估算价值。纳入获准的销售生产力、收入和质量指标。比较团队与模型，也比较工作流和用户群体。按回报与成本的比例排序。列出数据来源和公式，并明确说明假设、限制和缺失输入。不要声称这些结果是 ChatGPT 导致的。保持只读。</p> <p><strong>步骤</strong></p> <ol> <li><strong>准备：</strong>确认工作区和日期范围，再确认已批准的结果指标，并审查计算公式和隐私规则。</li> <li><strong>执行：</strong>请求 ROI 分析。</li> <li><strong>审查：</strong>检查每个来源和假设，并记录所有限制或缺失输入。</li> <li><strong>核实：</strong>仅凭使用情况无法证明 ROI 或因果关系。请与财务部门和业务负责人共同审查结果。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"assess-codex-roi\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"codex-roi\">评估 Codex 的 ROI</h3> <p><strong>可尝试的提示</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">For workspace {workspace_id}, combine verified Codex usage and cost from {date_range} with approved engineering outcomes. Estimate ROI by team, repository, and workflow. Compare productivity and delivery speed with code quality and engineering cost. Identify workflows that show high value or use many resources. Recommend changes to the model, reasoning mode, or workflow. Explain the tradeoffs and uncertainty. Present the findings as patterns in the available data, not proof that Codex caused the outcome. Return findings only; do not make changes.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>中文参考：</strong> 对工作区 {workspace_id}，将 {date_range} 内已核实的 Codex 用量和成本与获准使用的工程结果结合起来，按团队、代码库和工作流估算 ROI。比较生产力和交付速度，以及代码质量和工程成本。找出显示高价值或消耗大量资源的工作流。建议调整模型、推理模式或工作流，并解释取舍和不确定性。将发现表述为现有数据呈现的模式，而不是 Codex 导致结果的证明。只返回发现，不要进行更改。</p> <p><strong>步骤</strong></p> <ol> <li><strong>准备：</strong>确认工作区和报告期间，检查团队与代码库映射，以及已批准的基线数据。</li> <li><strong>执行：</strong>请求分析 Codex 的 ROI。</li> <li><strong>审查：</strong>区分观察到的模式和假设，并保护用户与代码库数据。</li> <li><strong>核实：</strong>与工程团队共同审查建议和结果基线。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"4-when-an-api-workflow-may-make-sense\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"4-api\">4. 何时可以考虑使用 API 工作流程</h2> <p>有些组织会使用 API 构建自己的管理流程或外部工具。这种方法适用于定期或持续运行的工作，也适用于需要处理大量记录或连接已批准内部系统的流程。它与 Admin 插件的引导式体验不同。</p> <p>先明确管理任务：列出所需输入和权限、审查节点、预期结果，以及结果的记录方式。如果组织要自动化此流程，应让相关的工程、安全和治理团队参与；将凭据保存在获准的密钥存储系统中，并在部署前测试工作流程。</p> <p><a id=\"related-resources\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_11\">相关资源</h3> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/public/admin/api-reference\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT 工作区 Admin API 参考（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8?anchor=understand-the-control-boundaries\">管理边界</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-88b1ced5fbccd242\">ChatGPT 工作区 Analytics API</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0\">ChatGPT 工作区 Compliance API</a></li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"using-the-admin-plugin-in-chatgpt-work\">Using the Admin plugin in ChatGPT Work</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Use this guide to understand how the Admin plugin supports common administration work, prepare for a task, and try prompts for key use cases with the right approvals and context.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=29SyCndnMZs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Watch: Admin plugin in ChatGPT Work (online)</a></p> <h2 id=\"1-understand-what-the-admin-plugin-is-for\">1. Understand what the Admin plugin is for</h2> <p>The Admin plugin is designed to help manage settings, permissions, and controls directly inside ChatGPT Work. You describe the goal in everyday language, and the plugin gathers the right inputs, reads the current state, explains what it finds, and guides the next supported step.</p> <h3 id=\"what-the-admin-plugin-is-designed-to-solve\">What the Admin plugin is designed to solve</h3> <ul> <li>Turn an admin request into a clear workflow without requiring you to write an API request.</li> <li>Review the current workspace state before making a decision or approving a change.</li> <li>Show which authorized sources and fields support the answer, along with anything it could not verify.</li> <li>Pause for review before a supported change, then read the record again to confirm the result.</li> </ul> <p>The plugin uses selected admin APIs and approved connected data sources behind the scenes. It does not combine every admin system, expand your permissions, or make every API action available in ChatGPT. The system that owns the data still controls what the plugin can read or change.</p> <h3 id=\"what-admin-apis-are-designed-to-solve\">What admin APIs are designed to solve</h3> <p>An admin API gives software a structured way to request data or a supported action. Organizations can use the admin APIs to build internal processes or external tools. Common examples include scheduled reports, repeated work across many records, and connections to approved systems. These workflows usually require engineering, security, and governance review.</p> <p>You do not need to build an API workflow to use this guide. The rest of the guide is centered on the Admin plugin. ChatGPT workspace administration and OpenAI API Platform administration also remain separate, with their own permissions and authentication requirements.</p> <h3 id=\"keep-credentials-private\">Keep credentials private</h3> <p>Use only your organization’s approved connections and secret-storage systems. Never paste a real admin API key into ChatGPT, Codex, a document, or a source file.</p> <h2 id=\"2-prepare-to-use-the-admin-plugin\">2. Prepare to use the Admin plugin</h2> <p>Use the Admin plugin for a supported, one-time task when you want to work through the request in everyday language. Describe the goal and provide the stable IDs or approved reporting context. The plugin shows what it found or what it plans to change before you decide whether to continue.</p> <p>The plugin uses only the sources, credentials, and actions authorized for that task. It does not combine every admin system or give you broader permissions. The original system remains the source of truth.</p> <h3 id=\"before-you-begin\">Before you begin</h3> <ol> <li>Find the admin area where the records live.</li> <li>Gather the required inputs and approval.</li> <li>Start with a read-only request.</li> <li>Ask the plugin which sources and fields it used, and what it could not verify.</li> <li>For a supported change, review the plan before you approve it. Then ask the plugin to read the record again and confirm the result.</li> </ol> <p>Confirm that the plugin is available in your workspace and that you have the required permissions. The role and access use cases below reflect the plugin’s current documented scope. The plugin can review roles, feature permissions, and user or group assignments. After you confirm, it can also assign an existing role to an existing group.</p> <p>The plugin cannot create roles, change a role’s permissions, or confirm access to a specific connector.</p> <p>The analytics use cases need access to connected, approved data sources. ROI analysis also needs approved business or engineering results; usage records alone are not enough.</p> <h2 id=\"3-explore-key-admin-plugin-use-cases\">3. Explore key Admin plugin use cases</h2> <p>Pick a use case, replace each placeholder with a value from your approved request, and follow the steps in order. Start with a read-only request unless the task is a supported change that already has approval.</p> <p>Use <a href=\"#/article/a-866d18fe9ed30c97?anchor=admin-bulk-migration\">Migrate custom GPTs in bulk</a> to inventory GPTs, migrate eligible batches, and coordinate owner testing and access checks.</p> <h3 id=\"list-workspace-roles\">List workspace roles</h3> <p><strong>Prompt to try</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">List the roles in workspace {workspace_id}. Separate built-in and custom roles. For each role, explain which features it can use and show the users or groups assigned to it. Don’t make changes.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Steps</strong></p> <ol> <li><strong>Gather:</strong> Confirm the workspace ID and that you are allowed to view this information.</li> <li><strong>Run:</strong> Ask for the read-only role list.</li> <li><strong>Review:</strong> Check the role types, feature access, and assignments.</li> <li><strong>Verify:</strong> Look into anything unexpected without making changes.</li> </ol> <h3 id=\"review-one-role\">Review one role</h3> <p><strong>Prompt to try</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Review role {role_id}. Explain its permissions in plain language, show who has it, and flag anything that looks broader than expected. Don’t edit the role.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Steps</strong></p> <ol> <li><strong>Gather:</strong> Confirm the role ID and workspace.</li> <li><strong>Run:</strong> Request the read-only role review.</li> <li><strong>Review:</strong> Check that the permissions and assignments match what the role is supposed to do.</li> <li><strong>Verify:</strong> Write down any questions for the role owner. Remember, the plugin cannot create the role or edit its permissions.</li> </ol> <h3 id=\"understand-a-users-or-groups-access\">Understand a user’s or group’s access</h3> <p><strong>Prompt to try</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Help me understand the access for user {user_id} or group {group_id}. Show their assigned roles, explain what access those roles provide, and point out overlaps or gaps. Clearly say what you can’t verify.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Steps</strong></p> <ol> <li><strong>Gather:</strong> Use the stable ID for the user or group.</li> <li><strong>Run:</strong> Ask the plugin to explain the access.</li> <li><strong>Review:</strong> Check which roles are assigned and what access they provide. Note any overlaps or gaps.</li> <li><strong>Verify:</strong> If the plugin cannot see something, mark it as unknown instead of guessing.</li> </ol> <h3 id=\"assign-an-existing-role-to-a-group\">Assign an existing role to a group</h3> <p><strong>Prompt to try</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Before making a change, show the current roles for group {group_id} and explain what role {role_id} would add. Confirm the recorded approver and wait for my explicit approval. After the assignment, verify the group’s updated roles.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Steps</strong></p> <ol> <li><strong>Gather:</strong> Confirm the group and role IDs. Check the approved request and recorded approver.</li> <li><strong>Run:</strong> Ask the plugin to show the current roles and what would change.</li> <li><strong>Review:</strong> Approve only if the plan matches the approved request.</li> <li><strong>Verify:</strong> After the assignment, check the group again to confirm that the existing role was added as approved.</li> </ol> <h3 id=\"check-general-connector-permission\">Check general connector permission</h3> <p><strong>Prompt to try</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Check whether user {user_id} has general connector access through their assigned roles. Ask the plugin to show which permissions support its answer. If it can’t verify access to a specific connector, have it say so clearly.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Steps</strong></p> <ol> <li><strong>Gather:</strong> Confirm the user ID and your permission to review the user’s access.</li> <li><strong>Run:</strong> Request the general permission check.</li> <li><strong>Review:</strong> Check the assigned role and the permission used for the answer.</li> <li><strong>Verify:</strong> Use this only as a general check. It does not prove access to a specific connector or connected item.</li> </ol> <h3 id=\"troubleshoot-an-approved-change\">Troubleshoot an approved change</h3> <p><strong>Prompt to try</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Review approved change {change_record_id}. Compare the requested result with the current workspace. If it failed, check the workspace and role first. Then confirm who owns the record, explain the issue, and suggest the safest next step.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Steps</strong></p> <ol> <li><strong>Gather:</strong> Confirm the approved change record and intended result.</li> <li><strong>Run:</strong> Ask the plugin to compare the request with the current workspace.</li> <li><strong>Review:</strong> Check the workspace and role. Next, verify the record owner.</li> <li><strong>Verify:</strong> Use the current workspace state as the source of truth before choosing the next step.</li> </ol> <h3 id=\"optimize-cost-and-model-mix\">Optimize cost and model mix</h3> <p><strong>Prompt to try</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">For {date_range} in workspace {workspace_id}, group verified token use and cost by use case. Compare models and reasoning modes using the speed and quality information available. Flag costly workflows when the data shows little evidence of value. Recommend where spending could be reduced or redirected toward work with stronger productivity or cost results. Include any approved revenue or quality signals. Estimate possible savings, explain tradeoffs, and separate verified observations from assumptions or missing inputs. Keep this read-only.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Steps</strong></p> <ol> <li><strong>Gather:</strong> Confirm the workspace, date range, and that cost data covers the full period. Check which approved performance or outcome fields are available.</li> <li><strong>Run:</strong> Ask for the cost and model comparison.</li> <li><strong>Review:</strong> Separate what the data shows from assumptions, missing inputs, and tradeoffs.</li> <li><strong>Verify:</strong> Check possible savings with Finance and the workflow owners before acting.</li> </ol> <h3 id=\"discover-usage-and-adoption\">Discover usage and adoption</h3> <p><strong>Prompt to try</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Analyze workspace {workspace_id} during {date_range}. Show tasks and token use by team and business function. Group cost by use case. Summarize what teams use ChatGPT and Codex to accomplish. Include examples from Legal, Marketing, and Sales. Compare available use of skills and plugins. Only report tool calls, connected apps, and multi-tool workflows if those fields are available. Show where teams use more advanced workflows and where there may be room to expand. Rank the top {5_or_10} use cases and show whether a small group of highly active users accounts for most usage. Don’t guess about activity that is not in the data.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Steps</strong></p> <ol> <li><strong>Gather:</strong> Check the workspace, date range, and team mappings. Make sure user-level reporting is approved.</li> <li><strong>Run:</strong> Ask for the usage and adoption analysis.</li> <li><strong>Review:</strong> Check which requested fields are available. Leave missing activity out rather than guessing.</li> <li><strong>Verify:</strong> High usage does not prove advanced use, business value, or individual performance.</li> </ol> <h3 id=\"measure-business-value-and-roi\">Measure business value and ROI</h3> <p><strong>Prompt to try</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">For workspace {workspace_id} in {date_range}, combine verified usage and cost with approved outcomes. Estimate value by team and use case. Include approved Sales measures for productivity, revenue, and quality. Compare teams and models, as well as workflows and user segments. Rank returns against cost. Show the sources and formula. Clearly state assumptions, limits, and missing inputs. Don’t claim ChatGPT caused the outcomes. Keep this read-only.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Steps</strong></p> <ol> <li><strong>Gather:</strong> Check the workspace and date range, then confirm the approved outcomes. Review the formula and privacy rules.</li> <li><strong>Run:</strong> Ask for the ROI analysis.</li> <li><strong>Review:</strong> Check every source and assumption. Note each limit or missing input.</li> <li><strong>Verify:</strong> Usage alone cannot prove ROI or causation. Review the result with Finance and business owners.</li> </ol> <h3 id=\"assess-codex-roi\">Assess Codex ROI</h3> <p><strong>Prompt to try</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">For workspace {workspace_id}, combine verified Codex usage and cost from {date_range} with approved engineering outcomes. Estimate ROI by team, repository, and workflow. Compare productivity and delivery speed with code quality and engineering cost. Identify workflows that show high value or use many resources. Recommend changes to the model, reasoning mode, or workflow. Explain the tradeoffs and uncertainty. Present the findings as patterns in the available data, not proof that Codex caused the outcome. Return findings only; do not make changes.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Steps</strong></p> <ol> <li><strong>Gather:</strong> Confirm the workspace and reporting period. Review the team and repository mappings and the approved baseline data.</li> <li><strong>Run:</strong> Ask for the Codex ROI analysis.</li> <li><strong>Review:</strong> Distinguish observed patterns from assumptions. Protect user and repository data.</li> <li><strong>Verify:</strong> Review recommendations and outcome baselines with Engineering.</li> </ol> <h2 id=\"4-when-an-api-workflow-may-make-sense\">4. When an API workflow may make sense</h2> <p>Some organizations build their own admin processes or external tools with the APIs. This approach can support scheduled or continuous work. It can also help when a process spans many records or needs to connect to an approved internal system. This is separate from the guided Admin plugin experience.</p> <p>Start with a defined admin task: identify the required inputs and permissions, review points, expected result, and how the outcome will be recorded. If your organization automates it, involve the appropriate engineering, security, and governance teams; keep credentials in approved secret storage; and test the workflow before deployment.</p> <h3 id=\"related-resources\">Related resources</h3> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/public/admin/api-reference\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT workspace Admin API reference (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8?anchor=understand-the-control-boundaries\">Administration boundaries</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-88b1ced5fbccd242\">ChatGPT workspace Analytics API</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0\">ChatGPT workspace Compliance API</a></li> </ul>"};
